# .gitattributes
#
# LF EVERYWHERE, in the index AND in the working tree.
#
# `eol=lf` is the load-bearing part and it is deliberately on the `*` line:
# without it, `text=auto` normalises on COMMIT but still hands the working tree
# CRLF wherever core.autocrlf=true, which is the Windows default. That split is
# not cosmetic here — `tools/optimize.mjs` hashes the RAW BYTES of every
# ENGINE_FILES member into the meta's engineHash, so a file whose only change is
# its line endings moves the hash and `tests/meta-schema.test.mjs` fails with no
# behaviour having changed at all. It has happened twice (commit c3d1736, and
# again on 2026-08-17 after a stash/restore cycle rewrote four engine files).
#
# Listing extensions individually was the old approach and it under-covered:
# .py, .yml and the dotfiles fell through to plain `text=auto`. One rule for
# everything cannot under-cover.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries git must never touch.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.db binary
*.zip binary
